summary:
  The shared round asks for each member's level at the member's own slot
  again, between the wait and the player.

history:
  The question is a blocking pactl, and the capture is read against the
  slot the member was told to play in, so whatever the answer took was
  added to that member's arrival and to nobody else's. On a synthetic
  clock on 2026-11-11, with two speakers both 100 ms from the microphone
  and 150 ms spent on the first one's query, the round read the second as
  150 ms early; with the same 150 ms on both it read nothing, which is
  how it hid. A query that ran into its own three-second timeout moved
  every later member off the schedule as well: plays at 0.75, 5.39, 5.39
  and 5.98 s where 0.6, 2.39, 4.18 and 5.98 were planned.
  The earlier test of this function answers the query in no time at all,
  and stayed green through all of it.

target:
  package/contents/ui/calibrate.py

find:
                           volumes[i], ultra_wav],

replace:
                           str(int(_ultra_volume_for(sink, trim))), ultra_wav],

expect:
  Killed by tests/test_calibrate.py::test_a_slow_level_query_on_one_speaker_is_not_read_as_that_speakers_lag.
  Line-neutral.
